## Phase-specific notes

### Decisions taken at sub-plan time (2026-05-08)

| Q | Decision | Why |
|---|---|---|
| react-query migration scope | **Keep all data hooks on vanilla client (incl. `useTasksData`).** `TrpcProvider` already mounts `QueryClientProvider`. | Audit: 173 files use `getTrpcVanillaClient()`, 0 use `trpc.X.useQuery/useMutation`. Rest of app is uniformly vanilla. Phase 4 done-criteria is "zero perceptible regression"; migrating one hook = inconsistent + risky. Infra mounted; phased migration is a future cleanup. `window.__slayzone_refreshData` contract preserved trivially. |
| Mode-switch reload | **`app.relaunch() + app.exit()`** | Embedded-server start/skip is a boot-time decision in Electron main. Full process restart = simplest correct semantics. |
| Auto-restart backoff | **Exp 1s/2s/4s/8s/16s, give up after 5 consecutive failures.** Reset counter after 60s of healthy uptime. | Standard. Surfaces toast on permanent failure. Healthy reset prevents flaky restarts over hours from triggering false-permanent. |
| Hidden-feature scope | **Skip hiding** in this phase. Browser panel + other Electron-only features remain visible in Remote mode; they fail gracefully when invoked (tRPC error / no-op). | User decision. Hide pass deferred. Master §11d already lists browser panel as a known Remote regression. |

### Mode-switch UX details

- New settings keys (local SQLite, via existing `settings` router):
  - `server_mode`: `'local'` (default) | `'remote'`
  - `remote_server_url`: full WS URL incl. `/trpc` path, e.g. `ws://box.lan:7800/trpc` (default `''`)
- Renderer boot: replace `getTrpcPort()` IPC call with new `getServerUrl()` IPC → returns `{ mode, url }`.
- If `mode==='remote'` and `remote_server_url` is empty/invalid, render a pre-mount `RemoteConfigScreen` (outside `TrpcProvider`) offering: enter URL → save+relaunch, OR switch back to Local → save+relaunch.
- Settings → new **Server** tab (between Data and Diagnostics):
  - Radio: Local / Remote.
  - URL input (enabled in Remote).
  - "Validate" button: probes `GET /health` (strip `ws://`→`http://`, drop `/trpc`).
  - "Save" persists via `settings.set` + shows confirm "Reload required" → calls new IPC `app.relaunch()` (= `app.relaunch()+app.exit(0)`).
  - Cancel discards.
- Validation is best-effort — server may be down at config time but reachable after relaunch. Mode switch always requires reload.
- Local SQLite stays opened in both modes for settings/theme/tab store. In Remote mode, `linearSyncPoller` / `discoveryPoller` / `taskEvents` listeners are skipped (their effects on local DB are pointless when remote owns data).

### Embedded-server auto-restart

- New module: `packages/apps/app/src/main/embedded-server-supervisor.ts`.
- Supervisor wraps `serverMod.startServer(...)`. On reject: schedule retry with `BACKOFF_MS[attempt]`, attempt++.
- After 5 fails: `notifyEvents.emit('embedded-server-failed', { attempts, lastError })` and stop. Surfaced to renderer via new `app.onEmbeddedServerFailed` tRPC subscription (mirrors `onSettingsChanged` pattern); renderer shows toast.
- On success: store handle, set timer that resets attempt counter after 60s of healthy uptime.
- **Crash detection scope**: only startup-time failures (port-in-use, DB lock, registration throw) are recoverable in-process. True post-start crashes via `uncaughtException` kill the whole Electron process and are out of scope here. Revisit if/when observed — matches master §11 deferral spirit.

### Hidden features in remote mode

Skipped in phase 4 per Q4 decision. Browser panel (WCV), file dialogs, reveal-in-finder, processes panel, devtools toggle, floating-agent global shortcut, etc. all remain visible. They will fail gracefully or no-op when invoked in Remote mode. Polished hide-pass = follow-up phase.

